; Sidearm. Local space matches every other weapon: barrel fires along -Z, +Y up.
;
; The shape is no longer primitives -- it is the pistol that came modelled with
; the soldier asset, pulled out of that file mesh by mesh and reassembled here.
; Its parts arrive pre-positioned relative to each other, so every one of them
; sits at identity inside Body; what Body does is turn the thing to face the way
; this game's weapons face and scale it from the asset's centimetres to metres.
;
; Everything around the mesh is unchanged and has to stay that way. The stats,
; the grip markers the hands solve onto, the sight line, the muzzle and its
; flash, and the two nodes the reload animates -- BoltHandle for the slide and
; Magazine for the magazine -- are the contract the rest of the game holds this
; to, whatever it happens to look like.
